  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthen Criminal Justice Actors</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">United Nations Office on Drugs and Crime (UNODC) will train criminal justice personnel (judges, magistrates, prosecutors, law enforcement, etc.) at the national and regional level in identified Southern African countries to increase the number of systematized, victim-centered human trafficking investigations and prosecutions. UNODC will conduct regional criminal justice personnel workshops to share promising practices in the successful investigation and prosecution of human trafficking cases. This project will ensure that all trainings include a victim-centered approach and build the capacity of criminal justice personnel to identify victims and refer them to the appropriate protection services. All trainings will include a training-of-trainers component and provide case consultation to training participants as needed.</narrative>
  </description>
